   U4’s identity and bound are valid. On each \(I_{q,b}\), the common admissible \(B\)-interval has length at most \(2\Delta<\ell\), contains at least \(\Delta-1\) weights, and loses at most one multiple of \(\ell\). Thus \(\omega(\ell)\ge\Delta-2\), with distinct inverse classes.

